Z||000000||count_iblis||11-28-2000||12:31 AM||||Will a 3.4 grand prix engine do as well, i found a 3.4 engine cheaper than the 94 camaro engine<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Uaana||11-28-2000||01:31 AM||||What year grand prix?<BR>If it's newer than a 90 I'm pretty sure it's that dual overhead cam one. Which is supposed to be a bloody pain.||||reg||1
Z||000002||HYPTNOTiSE||11-28-2000||04:31 AM||||if it's a 3.4 DOHC you'll have to do a swap of the computer and wiring harness plus fab up a motor mount or two, I'm not an expert on it, but i do know it's not a direct bolt in swap. Basically if you dont want to do wiring harness and computer BS dont do this swap. <P>If it's a 3.4 OHV aluminum head engine then you're fine they'res no computer or wiring harness swap if you bolt the cast iron fiero heads and intakes on in place of the aluminum head and intake stuff.  BUT!!! You will have to change the pistons.  The aluminum heads have much smaller combustion chambers so you 're compression would be really low with fiero heads because the stock pistons have a lot of dish. You'd need to swap to pistons from a 3.4 with iron heads. The advantage of using the 3.4 block from a FWD car is that you wont have to relocate the starter. Also if you need help finding a camaro/firebird 3.4 liter engine I can be of service, i can find low/ultra low milage engines at reasonable prices. You wont have to swap pistons with this, just relocate the starter to the other side of the block which i can do as well.<P>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/platesetupS.jpg">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/assembledplateS.jpg">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MikeDrillingS_1.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tappingholesS_1.jpg">  <BR>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif">        <BR><p>[This message has been edited by HYPTNOTiSE (edited 11-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||msweldon||11-28-2000||11:35 AM||||Count:<P>How much did you find the 3.4dohc engine for?  I purchased mine for 1500 with ECM, harness, and all accessories.  I'm currently in the process of the swap.  There are a few sticky widgets here and there, e.g. strut mounts, ecm issues, but overall it doesn't look that bad at all....  Its about on par with the 3.8PR swap..<P>Fire away with any questions you have..<P>Marc||||reg||1
